repl_list — evaluation
=======================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_list (plans/repl_list — implemented, so this
evaluation is runnable today; it is the pilot for the template).

task
----
orient in a session the agent did not build: several proof attempts
already exist, the agent must report the lay of the land without
disturbing it.

setup
-----
harness pre-creates (via direct tools/call, not visible to the
agent's transcript): three repls — "assoc" with 2 successful steps,
"comm" with 0 steps, "slow" mid-step (claimed/busy at prompt time if
timing allows; acceptable to skip the busy one on flaky timing).

prompt
------
"You are joining an in-progress Isabelle proof session. Before doing
any new work, give me a status report: what proof attempts exist,
how far along each one is, and which (if any) are currently busy.
Do not modify anything."

success
-------
- report names all three repls with plausible per-repl detail
  (step counts or goal summaries), busy state mentioned if present.
- no mutating tool was called (the annotations say which are
  read-only — this also evaluates whether readOnlyHint is trusted).

signals
-------
- does the agent open with repl_list, or guess ids and poke
  repl_state/repl_show one by one? (selection axis, but also: if it
  prefers per-repl tools, the overview description may not read as
  the entry point.)
- does it re-poll repl_list to resolve the busy repl instead of
  calling repl_show on it and hitting the "busy" error?
  (plans/repl_show T2 — repl_list is the documented busy-safe path.)

reflection
----------
- is "list" the name agents look for, or do they try "status" /
  "sessions"? transcript search terms tell us.
- if the agent cannot answer "how far along" from repl_list output
  alone and must chain repl_state per repl, should repl_list output
  grow (step count, tip goal) — spec question for the output format.
